   "project": "portfolio",
   "date": "2026-09-29",
   "source": "ITV Initial Tech Assessment Presentation to DOE 2026-09-29 .txt",
   "text": "Guidance (below is from this document, sent from Amy)\nPrimary Focus & Guidelines\nCore Objectives: Focus on quantifying the current energy/water/resource that could be impacted by the technology. Avoid discussing comparative technologies entirely-unless reputable, relevant, and peer reviewed (e.g. National Lab).\nTerminology: Moving forward, let’s frame the idea of target sectors to be more as \"spaces for opportunity\" rather than \"markets.\" (or “impacts”)\nDomain & Impact: For each technology, define the applicable domain (energy/water/waste), a quantification of applicable opportunity spaces (e.g., total water, energy consumption), and all potential applicable technology uses. \nNOTE: We are looking to capture ALL industrial applications for a particular technology.\nBaseline Energy (or whatever resource) Use: State applicable industrial energy (or whatever resource) use [xxx].\nEquations will likely be generalized across projects. The multiplier should also be included. \nMethodology (Secondary): Outline the formulas and scale up calculation approach (the specific variables and multipliers used)."
