   "source": "README.md",
   "text": "# Nick and Sam Assigned Projects Repository\n\nThis repository summarizes all projects assigned to Nick and Sam in the assignment workbook, and provides a project-by-project M&V approach grounded in the ITV cookbook.\n\n## Portfolio Overview\n| Project | Technology Provider | Host Site | Primary Application | Core KPI Focus | M&V Complexity | Evidence Confidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Armstrong at SVC (PepsiCo)](projects/armstrong-svc.md) | Armstrong International | SVC Manufacturing (PepsiCo) | Heat recovery and heat pump process heating | Fuel Use Ratio (Btu per gallon), utility savings | Medium | High |\n| [Birmingham HMC at Glidewell](projects/bhmc-glidewell.md) | Birmingham Hot Metal Coatings | Glidewell Specialties Foundry | Electric ladle preheating | Energy per preheat cycle, temperature uniformity, defect impacts | High | High |\n| [CEIA at Donaldson](projects/ceia-donaldson.md) | CEIA USA | Donaldson Company | Induction curing for filter assembly | Energy per earned production hour, quality equivalence | Medium | Medium |\n| [Element 16 at Searles Valley Minerals](projects/element16-svm.md) | Element 16 Technologies | Searles Valley Minerals | Sulfur thermal energy storage for process steam | Dispatched thermal energy, round-trip efficiency, levelized cost of heat | High | High |\n| [JoulesAI at Manus Bio](projects/joulesai-manus.md) | JoulesAI | Manus Bio | RL battery dispatch under real-time pricing | Total cost of electricity, price responsiveness, battery cycling quality | High | High |\n\n## Sector Analysis Matrix\n| Project | Sector | Process Profile | Why This Sector Fits the Technology | Scale-Up Potential |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Armstrong at SVC (PepsiCo)](projects/armstrong-svc.md) | Food and beverage manufacturing | Continuous thermal loads for pasteurization and sanitation | Heat pumps and recovery are strongest where steady low-to-mid temperature waste heat is available | High across beverage, dairy, and packaged food plants |\n| [Birmingham HMC at Glidewell](projects/bhmc-glidewell.md) | Metal casting and foundry operations | Batch high-temperature preheat cycles with quality-critical metallurgy | Electric preheating targets combustion losses and thermal uniformity in repetitive ladle duty cycles | Medium to high in iron and steel foundries with electrification drivers |\n| [CEIA at Donaldson](projects/ceia-donaldson.md) | Industrial filtration and discrete manufacturing | Repetitive adhesive curing with tight quality and takt-time constraints | Induction enables fast warm-up and localized heating in cure stations with high idle loss risk | High in adhesive-based assembly lines across manufacturing sectors |\n| [Element 16 at Searles Valley Minerals](projects/element16-svm.md) | Minerals and process industries | Large continuous steam demand and energy cost exposure | Thermal storage monetizes load shifting and decarbonization where industrial heat demand is persistent | High in minerals, chemicals, pulp and paper, and other steam-intensive sectors |\n| [JoulesAI at Manus Bio](projects/joulesai-manus.md) | Bioindustrial and chemical manufacturing | Dynamic electric loads with DER and battery dispatch opportunities | RL control is well matched to volatile pricing and multi-constraint operations | High across C&I sites with BESS, RTP tariffs, and controllable loads |\n\n## Quick Links\n- [Open the shared M&V framework](projects/mv-framework.md)\n- [Go directly to all project pages](#project-pages)"
